{
  "title": "A failed batch_block assignment silently forfeits the whole declare-blockers \
window instead of allowing a retry",
  "description": "Observed in game_20260831_093715 (Fable 5 vs Kimi K3, turn 6): Kimi K3 \
called choose_action(blockers=\"p10:p58\") to block a flying attacker with a \
non-flying/non-reach creature. BridgeChooseActionFlow.handleBatchBlockerTarget correctly \
rejects the illegal target (\"p10: attacker p58 is not a valid block target\"), but after \
cancelling it, advanceBatchBlockers exhausts the (one-item) assignment list and calls \
sendBooleanOrDie(action.gameId(), true, \"batchBlock:confirm\") at \
BridgeChooseActionFlow.java:324 -- confirming the declare-blockers step with zero blocks \
declared. The window to block is now permanently closed, but the error response never says \
so.\n\nKimi correctly diagnosed the problem (flying) and retried with a legal target \
(blockers=\"p10:p30\"), but by then the real pending decision had already moved to the \
post-combat priority window. The retry's blockers argument doesn't match a blockers-type \
prompt anymore, so it falls into the plain single-choice handler and fails with an \
unrelated, confusing error: \"GAME_SELECT requires choice=pN to play a card, or \
choice=\\\"no\\\" to pass priority.\" A get_game_state call made between the two attempts \
also still reported step=\"Declare Blockers\", so even careful state-checking wouldn't \
have revealed the window was already gone.\n\nNet effect: PilotB took all 8 unblocked \
combat damage despite describing (twice) a coherent, legal block plan -- not an LLM skill \
issue, a harness bug. Fix direction: the batch-blockers path should not auto-confirm an \
empty declaration just because one assignment in the list was illegal -- it should surface \
the failure and leave the window open for a corrected resubmission within the same \
choose_action call (or at minimum a subsequent one, if get_game_state still shows \
Declare Blockers). Failing that, the error message on a rejected retry should say the \
block window has closed rather than the generic GAME_SELECT complaint.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "bridge",
    "combat",
    "data-integrity",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-08-31T14:52:07.000000-07:00",
